<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_WastelandBrineScatter_Register.xml  UtinniPatches · authored 2026-09-18
  ============================================================================
  FISH_BESTIARY_BUILD_1 wave 2 — the registration half. RUT_WastelandBrineScatter.xml
  declares three GenStepDefs; a GenStepDef on its own runs on no map, the same
  fact RUT_ScaldWreckScatter_Register.xml (this same mod) already documents.

  SCOPE: Base_Player, GLOBAL — same justification RUT_ScaldWreckScatter_Register.xml
  already gives for its own three wreck GenStepDefs: each scatter step's OWN
  terrain validator (terrainValidationAllowed -> RUT_WastelandBrineShallow) already
  confines it to cells carrying that tag, and only the two RUT_WastelandBrine*
  shallow terrains (RUT_WastelandBrineWater.xml) carry it — nowhere else in the
  load order does. Registering onto Base_Player is still correct: the player's
  own settled map is where a brine-deposit scatter should visibly land.

  Target: Core/Defs/MapGeneration/BasePlayerMapGenerator.xml, MapGeneratorDef
  ParentName="MapCommonBase" Name="Base_Player", <genSteps> a plain list of
  GenStepDef names.

  No MayRequire needed on this patch — its three GenStepDefs are this mod's
  own, always loaded together with this patch. Conditional test xpath is
  identical to the inner Add's xpath, same discipline as its own precedent.

  Not held via DEPLOY_HOLD.txt: unlike RUT_ScaldWreckScatter_Register.xml, none
  of the three ThingDefs this patch's GenStepDefs name are missing art (see
  RUT_WastelandBrineDeposits.xml's own header) — nothing here is a dangling
  cross-reference.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/MapGeneratorDef[defName="Base_Player"]/genSteps</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/MapGeneratorDef[defName="Base_Player"]/genSteps</xpath>
      <value>
        <li>RUT_Jawa_ScatterWastelandBrineTekk</li>
        <li>RUT_Jawa_ScatterWastelandBrineDrazz</li>
        <li>RUT_Jawa_ScatterWastelandBrinePlate</li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
